WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.170
- Good day to you, Miss Cluckadoo.

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.310
(chickens clucking)

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.033
Might I examine your nesting box?

00:00:08.055 --> 00:00:10.700
(Suzanne exclaiming)

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.710
An egg is a tiny miracle, isn't it?

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.610
It's life and life's
sustenance all at once.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.423
- Okay, why are you so happy?

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.750
Did you get some new meds?
'Cause I want some of those.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.250
Unless they make you
speedy, 'cause I'm just

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.083
speedy enough as it is.

00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:27.830
- No, what you are seeing
is the joy a person feels

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.510
when they single-handedly,
through the power

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.740
of their own words, can turn the course

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.990
of another person's life.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:37.916
- Oh!

00:00:37.916 --> 00:00:39.415
- Look.

00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:40.248
Look.

00:00:41.957 --> 00:00:45.210
- "Dear Suzanne, thank you
for being a bull-headed,

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.653
refuse-to-listen-to-reason
pain in the ass."

00:00:48.653 --> 00:00:49.486
(laughs)

00:00:49.486 --> 00:00:51.680
"I think this book might actually help,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.367
so I'm sending it to my lawyer"?

00:00:56.127 --> 00:00:57.777
"I'm sorry I doubted
you in the first place."

00:00:57.777 --> 00:01:00.850
- "Your friend..."

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:01.683
Huh?

00:01:02.537 --> 00:01:03.370
"Taystee."

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:04.203
- Wow.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.620
That's really cool.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.110
- Yeah, it turns out I'm a fixer.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.973
Like Olivia Pope or Woodward
and Berenstain Bear.

00:01:15.027 --> 00:01:16.918
- [Lolly] Move chicken, chicken. Move.

00:01:16.918 --> 00:01:19.110
(chickens clucking)

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.040
- Hmm, only three?

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.310
Yet we have 12 chickens,
so it stands to reason

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.340
we should have closer to 12 eggs.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.810
Give or take.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.060
Ladies, gather around.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:31.320
It appears we have our
first chicken crisis.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.357
- A foul fowl?

00:01:32.357 --> 00:01:33.190
- Uh...

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:35.730
I'll allow it.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.820
Now, why are our chickens
not producing eggs?

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.200
- The eggs can get
stuck inside the cloaca.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.080
We could reach inside
and grab the eggs out.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.490
- Oh, maybe the chickens
are eating their own eggs.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.790
They're cannibal chickens.
It happens, you know!

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.700
- It does, but we would see
evidence of their abomination.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.433
I'm not seeing pecked-out shells.

00:01:53.433 --> 00:01:54.266
(Suzanne exclaims)

00:01:54.266 --> 00:01:55.900
- [Alvarez] Ms Warren? Your solve?

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.660
- They need sunlight.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.230
- Do chickens go through menopause?

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.090
'Cause we could make a
test of their hormones.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.260
- The coop is too dark and
the yard, it's covered.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.340
They need those harmful UVs.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.390
- Vitamin D is vital for egg production.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.720
- Mmm-hmm, yeah. The roof has gotta go.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.540
- That would leave them
vulnerable to predators.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.243
- What? Hello? We're in a prison.

00:02:17.173 --> 00:02:19.610
Do you not see that fence,
with the barbed wire on top?

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:20.530
There's nothing coming in.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:21.770
- Dragons!

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:22.603
- No.

00:02:22.603 --> 00:02:23.436
- Shh.

00:02:23.436 --> 00:02:25.540
- And, before you ask, they can't escape

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.609
because chickens can't fly.

00:02:27.609 --> 00:02:28.442
(laughs)

00:02:28.442 --> 00:02:30.300
- That's what they want you to think!

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.543
- All those in favor of opening the yard.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.060
Well, that's not a majority
but since it's the only

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.815
practical solution offered...

00:02:38.815 --> 00:02:39.713
- See?

00:02:41.001 --> 00:02:42.320
- Okay, okay, okay!

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.427
- I am a fixer!

00:02:43.427 --> 00:02:44.351
- You're a fixer.

00:02:44.351 --> 00:02:45.184
- A fixer.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.540
- [Alvarez] That's 10 eggs.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.620
A 233% improvement rate.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.210
I have to say, this sunlight
theory appears to have legs.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.410
Or should I say, eggs?

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.462
- I'll allow it.

00:02:59.462 --> 00:03:00.295
- Yeah?

00:03:00.295 --> 00:03:01.890
- I think you both mean drumsticks.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.620
- Either way, chicken crisis
averted, thanks to you.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.960
- [Suzanne] Thank you,
thank you. What can I say,

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.520
when I look into their chicken faces,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.930
I just understand them.
I think it's because

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:10.950
I think of them as people.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.600
- Chickens actually see
substantially better than people.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.650
They have two additional
cones, they can see colors

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.843
we can't even dream of.

00:03:16.843 --> 00:03:18.920
- Since one of the
tenets of farm therapy is

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.220
that taking responsibility for creatures

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.760
other than yourself
empowers you, Ms Warren,

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.020
you have earned the
position of Mayor of, uh,

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.481
New Cluck City.

00:03:29.481 --> 00:03:30.873
- What?

00:03:30.873 --> 00:03:33.610
Oh! I'm gonna need a podium and two flags

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:34.820
flanking me at all times.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:35.710
- New Cluck City? Nothing?

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:37.053
- It should have been me.

00:03:38.461 --> 00:03:40.213
- Thank you. Thank you for your service.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.358
Thank you. Oh...

00:03:43.358 --> 00:03:45.493
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:03:45.493 --> 00:03:47.730
Everything's-- Everything's changed.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.220
The responsibility...

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.980
Before, my life was...

00:03:52.831 --> 00:03:55.081
(exclaims)

00:03:56.637 --> 00:04:00.603
And now my life is the mayor.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:05.150
I promise to bring together
this divided house of chickens.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.673
I promise to fight for you.

00:04:07.671 --> 00:04:10.420
And for every citizen in this coop,

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:11.253
I promise to ensure--

00:04:11.253 --> 00:04:12.600
- Wait, wait, wait. Can I please...

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.793
May I please be your lieutenant?

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:18.823
- Yes.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:20.880
You can.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.713
- I can?

00:04:21.713 --> 00:04:22.689
- Yes, you can!

00:04:22.689 --> 00:04:23.539
Yes, you can!

00:04:23.539 --> 00:04:24.372
- Yes, I can!

00:04:24.372 --> 00:04:25.205
- Yes, you can!

00:04:25.205 --> 00:04:28.955
(imitating chicken clucking)

